@everyone we now have a 7 day free trial! Feel free to sign up on the sign, and hit the subscribe button. This will give you a 7 day free trial before you are charged and cancelling is as easy as one click on the “My Subscriptions” page!

Let me know what you guys think!

https://sortswift.com/

@everyone Don't miss out on the CSV Editor! More tools coming soon, and we can show you how to use the CSV Tools in our upcoming demo in a little over an hour!
https://discord.gg/hYK2P7XK?event=1287214693089546271

Don't miss it! If you have any questions this will be the place to ask! Support, Questions, Suggestions, Critique, all of it is welcome!

@everyone we are currently migrating our database to a larger server due to increased usage, this will improve speeds and reliability. We are moving from a 4x virtual cpus and 16gb ram to a dedicated 16 core with 32 threads and 196gb ram. We shouldn’t need to do this move again.

The site has been placed in maintenance mode until this database migration is finished, it could be 1-2 hours before complete.

Don’t worry, back end functions are still there, we just can’t have anyone adding more inventory in the masses for the time being.

@everyone
I wanted to share the Shopify App creation guide. Most of my time has been to do this for people, hopefully this guide sets it all up for you, if you have further questions, please reach out! I've also embedded this onto the Integrations page.
https://scribehow.com/shared/Create_the_Shopify_App_for_Integration__1Ftac6XcSV6SjdApI0FTxQ

@everyone
The SortSwift Demo is about to go live!
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GcapAHq4M4s

@everyone I would write a really long announcement message to say every thing that was changed in the latest push but I can’t write one up at this moment in time, there will be things added to the #change-logs channel as I get to it. POS major improvements, new theme adjustments, staging inventory, audit, and import logs adjustments to.

Along with Graded Cert lookup, and the frameworks for staff accounts, hopefully I can finalize the eBay testing and staff accounts testing and let you guys know good news very soon! 

Hopefully this short summary covered it all but there was a ton of improvements that I’m sure I’m forgetting. They’ll go to the change logs as I remember haha

@everyone CardTrader appears to be experiencing an outage.
Backend services still appear functional, but please monitor your sales for any related issues.

We’re actively monitoring the situation and will update once service is fully restored and work out if any damage control is required.

@everyone 
If you are interested in trying our shipping integration system (keep in mind it is live and “should” be functional), labels are functional and platform orders are imported. Please pm me and I’ll get you access. 

All platforms imported to one central interface and ship from that interface, but I need more eyes to get it perfected. I need quick responses and feedback because I want to implement and improve tonight for hopeful release tomorrow, (it needs launched before Monday morning)
